-- title:
--   Cusps other than ∞ carry a unit constant term (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime equal to $3$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, subject to the hypothesis that some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carries $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ (Laurent series over $L$) equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the rational $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the function field attached to $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$, together with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$ ($A \to L \to K$ a scalar tower). Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent series the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= \mathsf q^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } jNumQ)$. Write $A_\infty =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144), the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlg A (↥K) {j⁻¹}` of $K$, which contains the element $j^{-1}$ given by `jInvChartInf`. The assertion is: for every minimal prime $P$ of the ideal of $A_\infty$ generated by $j^{-1}$, if $P$ contains some element whose $\mathsf q$-expansion has non-zero coefficient in degree $0$, then $P$ contains an element $b$ whose degree-$0$ coefficient is not of the form $\mathrm{algebraMap}_{A\to L}(c)$ for any $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   This is the cusp-separation step on the pole chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $q = 3$: the minimal primes of $(1/j)$ are the cusps lying over $j = \infty$, and those distinct from the $\mathsf q$-adic cusp $\infty$ (detected by carrying a function with non-zero constant $\mathsf q$-coefficient) are shown to contain a function whose constant coefficient is a unit of $A$, so that such a prime does not survive the reduction used to cut out the cusp $\infty$. It is used in the proof that the localisation of the pole chart at the prime of the cusp $\infty$ is a regular local ring in the case $q = 3$.
-- source:
